---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Rainrail"
  description="Rainrail routes development events into deterministic agent workflows."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Event routing for agent operations</p>
      <h1>Rainrail turns development events into agent-ready workflows.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Connect GitHub issues, pull requests, project queues, and operational
        signals to repeatable automation without coupling every source to every
        runtime.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/how-it-works">See the flow</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/concepts">Read the concepts</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel event-flow" aria-label="Rainrail event flow">
      <div class="flow-step">
        <strong>Source event</strong>
        <span>GitHub, Cloudflare tail, project queues, and future adapters.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-step">
        <strong>Neutral envelope</strong>
        <span>Provider-specific payloads become a stable Rainrail event.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-step">
        <strong>Workflow dispatch</strong>
        <span>Plugins decide which agent workflow should handle the work.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-step">
        <strong>Runtime provider</strong>
        <span>Agents receive deterministic inputs and observable execution context.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Built for maintainable automation</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="item">
        <h3>Stable contracts</h3>
        <p>
          Event envelopes and plugin boundaries keep automation behavior explicit
          as source systems change.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <h3>Composable workflows</h3>
        <p>
          Source plugins, workflow plugins, and runtime providers evolve without
          collapsing into one provider-specific script.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <h3>Operational visibility</h3>
        <p>
          Dispatch decisions, assignment rules, and runtime context are designed
          to be reproducible and reviewable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Initial content</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="item">
        <h3><a href="/concepts">Concepts</a></h3>
        <p>
          Learn the event envelope, source plugin, workflow plugin, provider,
          and bridge room vocabulary before reading implementation contracts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <h3><a href="/guides">Guides</a></h3>
        <p>
          Follow the first GitHub issue automation, PR review loop, and
          Cloudflare event reporting paths at an operator level.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <h3><a href="/examples">Examples</a></h3>
        <p>
          Trace the GitHub issue to Project queue to agent PR to review and
          merge workflow end to end.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
